# Prefer existing UI before native HTML

Before writing a native control or one-off empty/loading/error block, check `components/ui` and `components/patterns` first.

## Controls (never invent)

| Need | Use |
|---|---|
| Select / dropdown | `@/components/ui/select` or `@/components/ui/dropdown-menu` |
| Date | `@/components/ui/date-picker` (or `calendar` + `popover`) |
| Dialog / sheet | `@/components/ui/dialog`, `@/components/ui/sheet` |
| Checkbox / input / textarea / button | matching `@/components/ui/*` |
| Segmented tabs | `@/components/ui/segmented-control` |

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<select value={v} onChange={…}><option>…</option></select>
<input type="date" value={v} onChange={…} />

// ✅ GOOD
import { Select, SelectContent, SelectItem, SelectTrigger, SelectValue } from '@/components/ui/select';
import { DatePicker } from '@/components/ui/date-picker';
```

## Async UI (never invent)

| State | Use |
|---|---|
| Loading | `Loader` / `Skeleton` — `@/components/patterns/loader`, `@/components/ui/skeleton` |
| Error | `ErrorState` — `@/components/patterns/error-state` |
| Empty | `EmptyState` — `@/components/patterns/empty-state` |
| Combined | `QueryState` — wraps Loader + ErrorState + EmptyState |

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
if (isPending) return <div className="animate-pulse">…</div>;
if (error) return <p>Failed</p>;
if (!rows.length) return <p>No data</p>;

// ✅ GOOD
<QueryState isPending={…} error={…} isEmpty={!rows.length} onRetry={…} loaderVariant="table">
  …
</QueryState>
```

## Also check first

- Tables / pagination → `DataTable`, `TablePagination`
- Page chrome → `PageHeader`, `StatusBadge`, `IconActionButton`
- Confirm / reason → `ConfirmDialog`, `ReasonDialog`

Only build a custom control when no existing primitive covers the interaction.
